  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;be vertices of a triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>P</mi></math> be a point on side <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#916;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#916;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;be the areas of triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>.</p><p>Respectively.</p><p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#916;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><msub><mi>&#916;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>7</mn></math>, then the area enclosed by the lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;and the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis is</p>",
